Finish the SCUS-94154 assists and the 60 FPS sustain guard.

Assists: gate every write to live play (the engine's timing mode at 0x8006CD14
is non-zero during demo playback and recording, so an attract loop could
previously be written into), add the third loop-signature word, and turn Aku
Aku into a three-level control: off / keep masks / no damage.

No damage holds the player's own invincibility mode. 0x8001CE1C is
`bne s0, a0` against the object at 0x8005F38C, so the predicate below it is the
player's alone; obj+0x108 is a timed mode (0x8001C0A8 gives mode 4 its 61 mercy
frames, 0x8001C0BC times mode 3, the gold mask). The assist holds mode 3 and
restamps obj+0x10C from the tick at 0x8006CB64 so it never expires, leaving
modes 1, 2, 5, 6 and 7 to the engine.

An instruction patch on 0x8001CE34 was tried first and REMOVED, because
psx_mod_write_code_word marks the whole containing page dirty and this runtime
dispatches dirty pages through the MIPS interpreter. func_8001CC10 runs for
every GOOL event on every object, so interpreting it collapsed the frame rate
until the starvation watchdog aborted the run - 8.4 s without a heartbeat. The
60 FPS gate survives the same trick only because its page is cold.

Overlay: the Home menu takes the mouse. The panel is drawn stretched over the
whole window, so window -> panel is a plain proportion; hover moves the cursor
without changing a value, left click activates, right click steps an option
back, and the wheel adjusts the row under the cursor.

The overlay's GAME ASPECT row also gains 14:9, which the launcher has always
offered and defaults to for this title - without it the Home menu could not
return to the aspect the game had launched in.

60 FPS stability, retuned for smoothness. The acceptance threshold was 85%,
which accepts one frame in seven being doubled - visible judder several times a
second - while reporting the scene as holding 60; it is 95% now, with the
forgive margin at 99%, so a scene that cannot keep nearly every frame on one
field gets a clean 30 instead of a ragged 56. The gate closes on the first bad
window (deciding slowly is paid in visible judder), then waits 20s, then 40s,
and latches after two back-offs; loads and 2D screens are their own verdict
rather than a silent pass, bank no credit, and release the latch because
whatever follows one is a different scene.

An automatic jump to 150% guest clock on a hold failure was added and then
removed: a measured sweep found no trustworthy improvement, and it fires in
exactly the scenes where the host is nearest its limit, so it produced the
stutter it was meant to cure. native_60fps_cpu_percent now defaults to 100.

60 FPS guard: drop two branches patch 0028 made unreachable - the CPU restore
on the sustained-good path (every reopen already sets the clock) and the
RETRY_MAX comparison (the shift is capped at 3 and 8000 << 3 is exactly that) -
set c2_60_suspended whenever the timing mode is non-zero rather than only on
the closing edge, reset the window on every suspended tick so demo frames stay
out of loop_hz and one_field_pct, and export the last verdict so a report can
tell a host overrun from a scene on the one-field boundary.

